# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Inkcast studio — environment
#
# EVERY VARIABLE HERE IS OPTIONAL. Copy this file to `.env.local` only if you
# want to opt into a cloud upgrade. With no `.env.local` at all the studio runs
# the fully local pipeline: heuristic planner, Kokoro ONNX voice, built-in icon
# set. That is the supported default path, not a fallback.
#
#   cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Where projects live ---------------------------------------------------
# Per-project working directories (`storyboard.json`, `audio/`, `frames/`,
# `out.mp4`). Relative paths resolve from the repo root. Consumed by
# @inkcast/core's `PROJECTS_ROOT`.
# INKCAST_PROJECTS=projects

# --- Logging ---------------------------------------------------------------
# One of: debug | info | warn | error. Shared with the CLI via
# @inkcast/core's `logger`.
# INKCAST_LOG=info

# --- Optional: cloud planning ----------------------------------------------
# Without this the planner uses its deterministic, structure-aware heuristic.
# With it, storyboard planning and natural-language storyboard edits go through
# Claude. Absence logs one warning line and degrades; it never crashes.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: cloud voice -------------------------------------------------
# Without this, narration is synthesised locally with Kokoro ONNX.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: cloud image synthesis ---------------------------------------
# Without these, visuals come from the built-in icon set plus procedural
# diagram layout. Set at most one.
# REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=
# FAL_KEY=

# --- Public (inlined into the browser bundle) ------------------------------
# Only set this if the studio is served from somewhere other than the origin
# the browser loaded it from. Never put a secret behind a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_INKCAST_BASE_URL=

# --- Optional: accounts ----------------------------------------------------
# Leave all of these unset and this deployment has no accounts: identity is a
# signed anonymous cookie, /studio and /library are open, and /sign-in and
# /sign-up return 404. That is the default and the supported path — docs/
# CONTRACT.md requires it, and it is what the landing page promises.
#
# Set BOTH of the first two and identity comes from Clerk instead: generating a
# video requires a sign-in, and the landing copy changes to say so. Exactly one
# of the two is treated as unset on purpose — a half-configured login is either a
# site that refuses everybody or a login page the server cannot verify.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE RIGHT PLACE FOR THEM. Next loads `apps/web/.env.local`
# itself; the repo-root `.env` is read by `apps/web/lib/store.ts`, which
# `proxy.ts` cannot import (it runs on the Edge runtime and that module uses
# node:fs). Clerk variables in the root `.env` only produce the confusing
# half-state where route handlers see accounts and the proxy does not.
#
# Get both from a Clerk instance's API keys page. Full walkthrough: docs/AUTH.md.
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...

# Where the shell's sign-in links point. Clerk's own variable names and Clerk's
# own defaults, so a tutorial-configured instance needs neither.
# WITHOUT THEM: /sign-in and /sign-up, which this app serves itself.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/sign-in
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL=/sign-up

# The account page — Clerk's hosted Account Portal, on a per-instance subdomain
# this app cannot derive. It is also the only way to sign out, because signing
# out needs Clerk's client SDK and a link cannot do it.
# WITHOUT IT: the nav shows an unlinked "Signed in" chip rather than pointing at
# a guessed URL, and there is no sign-out control in the app.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_ACCOUNT_URL=https://accounts.example.com/user

# --- Shared deployments only -----------------------------------------------
# Turns on the per-IP rate limiter, the 20k-character source cap, and the
# per-account encrypted key store. Leave it unset on a laptop.
# INKCAST_HOSTED=1
#
# REQUIRED when INKCAST_HOSTED=1, both of them. Each throws at import when it is
# missing on a hosted box, so the deployment fails loudly at startup instead of
# quietly serving forgeable cookies or refusing to encrypt a credential.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# INKCAST_SESSION_SECRET=
# INKCAST_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Stateless hosting (Vercel) ---------------------------------------------
# Projects, progress and films in Vercel Blob; rendering on the render service
# (apps/render-service, deployed from Dockerfile.vercel). Leave all of these
# unset everywhere else. Full setup and the env matrix: docs/DEPLOY_VERCEL.md.
# INKCAST_STORAGE=blob
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=          # set by Vercel when a Blob store is connected
# INKCAST_BLOB_PREFIX=inkcast
# INKCAST_BLOB_ACCESS=private
# INKCAST_RENDER_URL=https://inkcast-render.vercel.app
# INKCAST_RENDER_TOKEN=           # openssl rand -hex 32; same value on the render project
# INKCAST_RENDER_BYPASS_TOKEN=    # only if the render project is behind Deployment Protection
